WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.467 --> 00:00:02.035
Oren you just heard the president saying

00:00:02.035 --> 00:00:03.169
that Secretary Austin,

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:03.970
General Austin,

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:04.838
former general, now

00:00:04.838 --> 00:00:06.172
the secretary of defense

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:07.107
recommended this.

00:00:07.107 --> 00:00:08.675
But we've talked in recent weeks

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:09.743
about how the Pentagon

00:00:09.743 --> 00:00:10.877
was somewhat resistance

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:12.846
because of the logistics involved,

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:13.913
because of the

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:17.217
the resupply and the keeping, the tanks

00:00:17.217 --> 00:00:18.451
and the training involved,

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:18.952
how quickly

00:00:18.952 --> 00:00:20.020
the American tanks get there,

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:20.987
and how big of a difference

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:22.722
does the Pentagon think they can make?

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:23.423
The short answer

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:25.025
that is not quickly at all.

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:26.126
These have to be procured

00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:27.460
and then you have to train the Ukrainians

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.129
on logistics, maintenance

00:00:29.129 --> 00:00:31.331
operations of a complex system.

00:00:31.331 --> 00:00:33.199
And that's on top of all the new systems

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:34.601
you already need to train them

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:35.168
on the U.K.

00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:36.202
Challenger tanks,

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:37.404
the German leopard tanks,

00:00:37.404 --> 00:00:38.805
us Paladin Howitzers,

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:40.206
the Patriot missile system.

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:41.341
So it's not a rush

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:42.442
to get these to the front.

00:00:42.442 --> 00:00:43.510
The other systems

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:44.110
and Germany's

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:46.046
leopard tanks are their priority.

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:47.213
But Biden did say

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:48.782
they would begin training

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:50.150
Ukrainian forces on the Abrams

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:50.550
to make sure

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.985
that when they're ready to go,

00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:53.453
Ukrainians can use them immediately

00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:55.021
when they arrive in country.

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:57.357
John on leave the Pentagon, thank you.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:58.792
Let's continue the conversation

00:00:58.792 --> 00:01:00.427
bringing two of our best.

00:01:00.427 --> 00:01:01.461
Nick Paton Walsh joins us

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:02.328
live from London.

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:04.798
General Mark Hertling joins us as well.

00:01:04.798 --> 00:01:06.099
Nick, I want to start with you.

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:07.500
You wrote a fantastic piece

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.669
about the strategic implications of this

00:01:09.836 --> 00:01:10.804
for CNN.

00:01:10.804 --> 00:01:11.404
It's on the Internet.

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:12.138
I urge everybody

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:13.306
to go to see an intercom and read it.

00:01:13.306 --> 00:01:14.774
You say this, among other things,

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:16.409
it is a momentous decision, partly

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:18.511
because these are not defensive weapons.

00:01:18.545 --> 00:01:19.879
They are intended to hit

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:20.513
Russia's troops

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:21.848
hard in a ground offensive.

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:23.083
They are unequivocally

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:25.051
about Ukraine retaking territory.

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:26.653
This is a new and fierce

00:01:26.653 --> 00:01:28.721
and it portrays a NATO's unafraid

00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:30.924
this is its help for Zelensky

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:32.125
that is long asked for.

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:33.660
But this is, as the United States

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:35.395
has said, a message to Vladimir Putin,

00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:36.362
You thought we would blink.

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:37.831
You thought we would crumble.

00:01:37.831 --> 00:01:39.566
Just the contrary.

00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:39.799
Yeah.

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:41.067
And it is frankly hard to say

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:41.768
after the weeks

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:42.068
in which

00:01:42.068 --> 00:01:42.769
we've seen

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:44.237
this diplomatic tussle

00:01:44.237 --> 00:01:46.239
with Germany reluctant

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:48.241
to give authorization for leopards

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:50.009
to be used, manufactured in Germany,

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:52.045
now being portrayed as kind of the leader

00:01:52.045 --> 00:01:53.113
of this European effort

00:01:53.113 --> 00:01:54.080
by Joe Biden,

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:55.148
they're getting Lepre

00:01:55.148 --> 00:01:57.350
thanks to Ukraine as quickly as possible.

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:58.685
Fundamentally, at the end,

00:01:58.685 --> 00:02:01.121
another sign of Western unity.

00:02:01.121 --> 00:02:03.123
Now, Joe Biden was clear there to talk

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:03.823
about how

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:04.691
this is not

00:02:04.691 --> 00:02:06.459
an offensive capability,

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:07.360
suggesting essentially

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:07.827
that Ukraine

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:09.129
is always defending itself,

00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:10.497
even when it goes on the offensive

00:02:10.497 --> 00:02:12.632
inside its territory to kick Russia out.

00:02:12.866 --> 00:02:13.600
A valid argument,

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:14.634
I think you would say,

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:15.268
but certainly

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:16.236
it shows that the West

00:02:16.236 --> 00:02:17.704
is no longer concerned

00:02:17.704 --> 00:02:20.240
about giving elements of its weaponry,

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.108
which it might have closely guarded,

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:23.476
to potentially defend itself

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:25.478
from an escalation by Russia.

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:27.280
It does appear that most of those nations

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:28.982
giving forward their advanced weaponry

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:29.949
don't think they're necessarily

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:31.351
going to need it to defend themselves

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:32.952
in an escalation of conflict

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:34.821
in the months or years ahead.

00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:35.822
And it also suggests

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:37.090
that this consistent drip

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:38.191
feeding from the Kremlin,

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:40.760
the idea that some sort of escalation

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:41.561
might follow

00:02:41.561 --> 00:02:43.763
if the West crossed some red lines

00:02:43.763 --> 00:02:45.165
that weren't to Russia's liking,

00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:45.965
then they're not really afraid

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:46.633
of that anymore,

00:02:46.633 --> 00:02:48.434
that they've heard the nuclear rhetoric.

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:50.003
They've challenged it openly.

00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:51.771
They've signaled against Russia's

00:02:51.771 --> 00:02:53.273
sort of nuclear blackmail,

00:02:53.273 --> 00:02:54.841
as some have referred to it.

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:56.042
And they might start to begin

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:58.411
to wonder now what else could happen.

00:02:58.478 --> 00:02:59.846
It's important to point out, though,

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:00.480
that these tanks

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:01.681
are not suddenly going

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:02.549
to turn up overnight

00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:04.651
and radically change the battlefield.

00:03:04.651 --> 00:03:06.486
There aren't that many initially pledge

00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:08.755
they will take months to put into

00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:09.889
training, certainly.

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:10.757
And Joe Biden

00:03:10.757 --> 00:03:11.991
there was keen to point out

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:12.559
that there'll be a lot

00:03:12.559 --> 00:03:14.594
of training happening now for Ukrainians

00:03:14.594 --> 00:03:16.729
to be able to get these complex

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:18.631
logistical systems up and ready.

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:19.899
This is a huge country

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:21.467
with vast amounts of terrain

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:23.703
to fight over and to take tanks

00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:24.270
back,

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:25.438
potentially to repair

00:03:25.438 --> 00:03:27.941
depots that need some kind of refit.

00:03:27.941 --> 00:03:29.709
So a huge task ahead.

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:31.511
But it does do one important thing,

00:03:31.511 --> 00:03:33.046
and it tells those in Moscow

00:03:33.046 --> 00:03:34.581
planning the months ahead

00:03:34.581 --> 00:03:36.149
that they have a very small window

00:03:36.149 --> 00:03:37.016
until Ukraine's

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:38.451
weaponry gets incrementally

00:03:38.451 --> 00:03:40.653
and enormously better in its quality.

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:41.454
And that is something

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:42.622
I'm sure that will be weighing

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:43.756
on the morale of those

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:45.058
in Russia's military.

00:03:45.058 --> 00:03:46.826
General Hertling, come in on that point.

00:03:46.826 --> 00:03:47.961
Your distinguished resumé

00:03:47.961 --> 00:03:49.796
includes commander, U.S. forces, Europe.

00:03:49.796 --> 00:03:51.664
So you understand the capabilities here.

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:53.933
You also understand the terrain here.

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:56.603
What is the military significance here

00:03:56.603 --> 00:03:57.837
on the battlefield?

00:03:57.837 --> 00:03:59.372
And what message is Nick just notes,

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:00.173
does it send to Putin?

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:02.542
Well, I'm impressed

00:04:02.542 --> 00:04:04.110
by everyone's commentary on this,

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:05.845
because you're getting it mostly right,

00:04:05.845 --> 00:04:08.047
John, both you and Nick and what I'd say,

00:04:08.047 --> 00:04:08.648
tanks are

00:04:08.648 --> 00:04:10.416
primarily used for tactical

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:11.918
offensive operations,

00:04:11.918 --> 00:04:14.087
shock action, rapid maneuver,

00:04:14.087 --> 00:04:15.622
lethal firepower.

00:04:15.622 --> 00:04:16.956
They are both physically

00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:18.791
and psychologically intimidating

00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:19.592
when used.

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:20.560
But here's the key point

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:22.395
when used correctly,

00:04:22.395 --> 00:04:24.163
and that requires the training

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:25.965
when we're talking about the numbers

00:04:25.965 --> 00:04:26.332
that have been

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:28.301
bandied around this morning,

00:04:28.301 --> 00:04:30.303
the president just said that

00:04:30.303 --> 00:04:32.071
Germany is providing

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:34.340
two tank battalions worth of equipment

00:04:34.741 --> 00:04:35.575
a German tank

00:04:35.575 --> 00:04:37.343
battalion is about 44 tanks.

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:38.945
So maybe you're talking

00:04:38.945 --> 00:04:40.980
80 tanks from Germany.

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:43.483
There are 13 other allied and partner

00:04:43.483 --> 00:04:44.917
nations in Europe

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:46.452
that also use the Leos,

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:47.754
the Leopard, two tanks.

00:04:47.754 --> 00:04:49.322
So you could see other ones

00:04:49.322 --> 00:04:50.056
like Poland

00:04:50.056 --> 00:04:50.757
and other

00:04:51.157 --> 00:04:53.726
other countries jumping on the bandwagon.

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:55.161
President Biden mentioned

00:04:55.161 --> 00:04:57.463
the US is giving 31 Abrams

00:04:57.697 --> 00:04:59.065
that's one Ukrainian

00:04:59.065 --> 00:05:01.100
battalion three companies of ten

00:05:01.267 --> 00:05:02.702
plus an additional tank

00:05:02.702 --> 00:05:04.137
for the battalion commander.

00:05:04.137 --> 00:05:06.773
So we're talking about certainly

00:05:06.773 --> 00:05:08.107
a lesser number

00:05:08.107 --> 00:05:09.375
than General Zelinsky

00:05:09.375 --> 00:05:11.411
the chief of the Ukrainian ground

00:05:11.411 --> 00:05:14.280
forces wanted he asked for 300 tanks.

00:05:15.214 --> 00:05:16.282
I've kind of thought

00:05:16.282 --> 00:05:17.917
that he's the maximum

00:05:17.917 --> 00:05:18.951
they're going to get into

00:05:18.951 --> 00:05:22.689
Ukraine is about 100 to 150 early on

00:05:23.022 --> 00:05:24.991
But the thing is is as Nick

00:05:24.991 --> 00:05:26.225
just pointed out,

00:05:26.225 --> 00:05:28.094
this is going to take a long time.

00:05:28.094 --> 00:05:30.096
The German Leos are a short

00:05:30.129 --> 00:05:31.331
term solution.

00:05:31.331 --> 00:05:33.032
They can train up on them.

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:35.001
It's a simple diesel

00:05:35.001 --> 00:05:36.736
engine weapon system.

00:05:36.736 --> 00:05:38.404
There is transfer ability.

00:05:38.404 --> 00:05:40.473
Like Sam said, it's more how I ride.

00:05:40.673 --> 00:05:41.874
I'd counter what Sam said.

00:05:41.874 --> 00:05:43.076
It's more than just learning

00:05:43.076 --> 00:05:44.510
how to drive the tanks.

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:46.145
There's a lot of mechanics involved

00:05:46.145 --> 00:05:47.380
and resupply

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:49.482
and recovery opportunities here.

00:05:50.049 --> 00:05:52.452
The Abrams is much more complex

00:05:53.252 --> 00:05:55.021
and that's a longer commitment

00:05:55.021 --> 00:05:55.988
to Ukraine.

00:05:55.988 --> 00:05:57.256
The leaders are probably going

00:05:57.256 --> 00:05:59.359
to get there within two to three months.

00:05:59.359 --> 00:06:00.393
The Abrams,

00:06:00.393 --> 00:06:02.362
you know, I'd put the estimate on that

00:06:02.362 --> 00:06:03.229
in terms of the

00:06:03.229 --> 00:06:03.730
what I know

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:06.165
about maintaining and logistics

00:06:06.332 --> 00:06:07.633
support for Abrams.

00:06:07.633 --> 00:06:08.134
I'm going to say

00:06:08.134 --> 00:06:09.102
that's a longer term

00:06:09.102 --> 00:06:10.636
commitment to Ukraine's

00:06:10.636 --> 00:06:12.672
continued military transformation.

00:06:12.672 --> 00:06:14.107
It's going to take between six

00:06:14.107 --> 00:06:14.741
to eight months

00:06:14.741 --> 00:06:16.609
for those vehicles to get there.

00:06:16.609 --> 00:06:19.412
So a reminder, reminder, as we approach

00:06:19.412 --> 00:06:20.613
the one year anniversary

00:06:20.613 --> 00:06:21.581
of the beginning of this war

00:06:21.581 --> 00:06:22.815
that everybody expects it

00:06:22.815 --> 00:06:24.717
to go well into a second year

00:06:24.717 --> 00:06:25.852
as well as we go through this.

00:06:25.852 --> 00:06:26.386
General Hurley,

00:06:26.386 --> 00:06:27.720
Nick Paton Walsh, grateful

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:28.988
for the important insights.

00:06:28.988 --> 00:06:29.522
And we'll continue

00:06:29.522 --> 00:06:30.623
to stay on top of this story

00:06:30.623 --> 00:06:31.224
as the tanks

00:06:31.224 --> 00:06:32.725
now will be delivered to the battlefield

00:06:32.725 --> 00:06:34.327
in Ukraine in the days, weeks and

00:06:34.327 --> 00:06:34.994
months ahead.

